title: 'sp-state-machine: roll back transaction index operations together with storage'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Index operations requested by the runtime through `transaction_index::index` and
    `transaction_index::renew` were kept when the storage transaction they were made in was
    rolled back. A reverted call, for example a `store` inside a failed `batch_all`, still made
    the node index its data, although the runtime kept no record of it.

    `OverlayedChanges` now drops the index operations of a rolled back transaction, the same way
    it already drops its storage changes.
crates:
- name: sp-state-machine
  bump: patch
